    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 22 tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS), including the new `Cp13Tests`. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `namesakeCount` field on owner creation. When an owner is created via `POST /api/owners`, the response (and subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}`) now returns `namesakeCount` = the number of existing owners (before this create) whose `firstName` **and** `lastName` match, compared case-insensitively.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a `countNamesakes(firstName, lastName)` helper that counts existing owners via `clinicService.findAllOwners()` using `equalsIgnoreCase`, called before the new owner is saved so the new owner itself is never counted. The result is set on the owner with `owner.setNamesakeCount(...)`.\n\n2. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added a persisted `namesakeCount` field (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`) with getter/setter, so it survives the save/read-back round trip.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `namesakeCount` integer property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically.\n\n4. **Schema files** \u2014 added a `namesake_count` column to the `owners` table in all four DB dialects (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`). The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema column is required there.\n\nVerified: `Cp13Tests` passes and the full suite is green (22 tests, BUILD SUCCESS).",
